<section class="section">
  <div class="container narrow prose">
    <h2>The story so far</h2>
    <p>I grew up in Eastbourne, as well as Glasgow, Billericay and Bexhill. Like a lot of people, I then moved to London for work and stayed for 13 years. There I built websites, looked after computer systems and led technical teams for organisations such as Barclays, British Airways and HSBC.</p>
    <p>In all, I've worked in IT for more than 25 years. The sea kept calling, though, and eventually we moved back. Now I live here with my family and our cockapoo, and on a good day you'll find me sea swimming or walking on the South Downs.</p>
    <p>Technology is now part of everyday life: the doctor, the bank, the shopping, keeping in touch with family. Plenty of people don't need a salesperson or a helpline. They need someone patient who'll explain things properly and never make them feel silly. That's what I offer.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section section-tint" aria-labelledby="legit-heading">
